.TH tkufiledialog n 0.3 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkufiledialog
.PP
Modal \fBopen / save / directory\fR chooser on top of \fBtkupath\fR + \fBtkufilelist\fR. Same look as the explorer stack; local \fBtuprovider\fR by default, optional \fB\-provider\fR for ZIP/remote. On the left \fBPlaces\fR: the home folder and the user folders, drives or the root, and \-\- with \fB\-app\fR \-\- bookmarks and recent folders. Returns a path (or a list with \fB\-multiple\fR), or \fB""\fR / \fB{}\fR if cancelled. Tk 8.6+ and 9.x.
.PP
Not a full file manager — a compact dialog for “pick this file/folder”.
.SS API
.CS
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::open      ?options?
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::save      ?options?
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::directory ?options?
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::bookmarks    app        ;# list of {label path}
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::setBookmarks app list   ;# replace them
.CE
.SS Options
.TS
l l.
Option	Meaning
\fB\-parent w\fR	toplevel for transient / placement
\fB\-title t\fR	window title
\fB\-initialdir d\fR	start directory (default: the last one with \fB\-app\fR, else \fB$HOME\fR or \fBpwd\fR)
\fB\-provider p\fR	\fBtuprovider\fR (default: fresh local)
\fB\-filetypes {{Label {.ext …}}…}\fR	type combobox → list filter; every extension of a type counts
\fB\-multiple 0|1\fR	open only: return a list of paths
\fB\-showhidden 0|1\fR	show hidden files (the dialog has a check box for it)
\fB\-showsystem 0|1\fR	Windows: also show hidden system files
\fB\-hideextensions 0|1\fR	hide known extensions in the names
\fB\-columns keys\fR	columns of the list (\fBname mtime type size ext\fR)
\fB\-timeformat f\fR	\fBclock format\fR of the Modified column
\fB\-app name\fR	remember bookmarks, recent folders, last folder, view and size for this application
\fB\-places 0|1\fR	the Places pane (default 1; only with the local provider)
\fB\-initialfile name\fR	save only: prefill name entry
\fB\-defaultextension .ext\fR	save only: append if name has no extension
.TE
.SS Behaviour
.IP \(bu
Double\-click a \fBdirectory\fR → navigate; double\-click a \fBfile\fR → OK (open/save).
.IP \(bu
Escape / Cancel → empty result; OK / Return in the name field → confirm.
.IP \(bu
Directory mode lists folders only; OK returns the selected folder or the current path.
.IP \(bu
\fBShow hidden files\fR at the bottom switches hidden files on and off. On Windows, protected system files (hidden \fBand\fR system, such as \fBdesktop.ini\fR) stay hidden, as in the Explorer; only \fB\-showsystem 1\fR in the call shows them.
.IP \(bu
A right\-click on the column headers shows and hides columns.
.IP \(bu
\fBPlaces\fR (local provider only): Home, Desktop, Documents, Downloads \-\- on Linux the folders named in \fB~/.config/user\-dirs.dirs\fR, so a German "Schreibtisch" is found; on Windows the folders from the registry (\fBUser Shell Folders\fR, read only), so a Desktop moved to OneDrive is found \-\- then the drives (Windows; not Tcl 9's \fB//zipfs:/\fR) or the root.
.SS "Bookmarks and settings (\fB\-app\fR)"
.PP
With \fB\-app name\fR the dialog keeps, per application, in the config directory of \fBname\fR (\fBtclutils::tusettings\fR: \fB%APPDATA%\ename\fR, \fB~/.config/name\fR, \fB~/Library/Application Support/name\fR):
.IP \(bu
\fBfiledialog.ini\fR \-\- the bookmarks, the view (columns, hidden files, extensions, sorting), the window size and the last folder;
.IP \(bu
\fBfiledialog\-dirs.txt\fR \-\- the last ten folders confirmed with OK.
.PP
"+ Bookmark this folder" adds the current folder, once: paths are compared normalized, on Windows without regard to case. A right\-click on a bookmark offers Rename and Remove. A bookmark or recent folder that no longer exists (a USB stick pulled out) is shown grey and kept. Without \fB\-app\fR nothing is written. An option given in the call wins over the saved view.
.SS Use
.CS
package require tkutils::tkufiledialog

set f [::tkutils::tkufiledialog::open -parent . -app myapp \
    -title "Open text" -filetypes {{Text {.txt .md}} {All *}}]

set d [::tkutils::tkufiledialog::directory -parent . -initialdir /tmp]

set s [::tkutils::tkufiledialog::save -parent . -app myapp \
    -initialfile out.txt -defaultextension .txt]
.CE
.SS Texts
.PP
Labels are English and go through \fBmsgcat\fR (namespace \fB::tkutils\fR), like \fBtkufilelist\fR: \fBPlaces\fR, \fBBookmarks\fR, \fBRecent\fR, \fBHome\fR, \fBDesktop\fR, \fBDocuments\fR, \fBDownloads\fR, \fBComputer\fR, \fB+ Bookmark this folder\fR, \fBShow hidden files\fR, \fBRename...\fR, \fBRemove\fR, \fBRename bookmark\fR, \fBOpen\fR, \fBSave\fR, \fBChoose folder\fR, \fBName\fR, \fBFolder\fR, \fBType\fR, \fBOK\fR, \fBCancel\fR, \fBAll files\fR.
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtkufilelist\fR, \fBtkupath\fR, \fBtkudialog\fR, \fBtclutils::tuprovider\fR, \fBtclutils::tusettings\fR
